{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0172ae35jThvgsGf12Um31xm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# dict\n2\tdict in pure C with runtime generic\n3\t\n4\t## How to install\n5\t```\n6\tgit clone https://github.com/wrnlb666/dict.git\n7\tcd dict\n8\tmake\n9\t```\n10\t\n11\t## Example for quick start\n12\t```c\n13\t#include \"src/dict.h\"\n14\t#include <stdint.h>\n15\t#include <inttypes.h>\n16\t\n17\t// define `dict_double` for not needing to cast the return value of `dict_get`. \n18\t#define dict_double( dict, key ) ( *(double*) dict_get( dict, key ) )\n19\t\n20\tint main( void )\n21\t{\n22\t    // create a new dictionary with key type int32_t, and value type double. \n23\t    dict_t* dict = dict_new( DICT_I32, sizeof (int32_t), sizeof (double) );\n24\t\n25\t    // iterate 30 times and add 30 items into the dictionary\n26\t    for ( int32_t i = 0; i < 30; i++ )\n27\t    {\n28\t        dict_double( dict, i ) = (double)i;\n29\t    }\n30\t\n31\t    // iterate 30 times and print the values. \n32\t    for ( int32_t i = 0; i < 30; i++ )\n33\t    {\n34\t        printf( \"[key]: %2\" PRId32 \", [val]: %5lf\\n\", i, dict_double( dict, i ) );\n35\t    }\n36\t\n37\t    // destroy the dictionary, free up the memory used by it. \n38\t    dict_destroy( dict );\n39\t\n40\t    return 0;\n41\t}\n42\t```\n43\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a2e6f3c-6ad8-4292-9b70-280d91438432","uuid":"de3038a8-e0cf-45a8-9493-e50a012eb80b","timestamp":"2026-06-05T22:39:04.607Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-31062124/harvest-crust-Su5Tmi/project/c_src/README.md","content":"# dict\ndict in pure C with runtime generic\n\n## How to install\n```\ngit clone https://github.com/wrnlb666/dict.git\ncd dict\nmake\n```\n\n## Example for quick start\n```c\n#include \"src/dict.h\"\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <inttypes.h>\n\n// define `dict_double` for not needing to cast the return value of `dict_get`. \n#define dict_double( dict, key ) ( *(double*) dict_get( dict, key ) )\n\nint main( void )\n{\n    // create a new dictionary with key type int32_t, and value type double. \n    dict_t* dict = dict_new( DICT_I32, sizeof (int32_t), sizeof (double) );\n\n    // iterate 30 times and add 30 items into the dictionary\n    for ( int32_t i = 0; i < 30; i++ )\n    {\n        dict_double( dict, i ) = (double)i;\n    }\n\n    // iterate 30 times and print the values. \n    for ( int32_t i = 0; i < 30; i++ )\n    {\n        printf( \"[key]: %2\" PRId32 \", [val]: %5lf\\n\", i, dict_double( dict, i ) );\n    }\n\n    // destroy the dictionary, free up the memory used by it. \n    dict_destroy( dict );\n\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n","numLines":43,"startLine":1,"totalLines":43}}}
